    <Section eyebrow="Assumptions and non-guarantees" title="Keep the model honest.">
      <div className="grid two"><Card title="Required foundations" icon="shield" tone="mint"><p>Correct conditional create/overwrite, read-after-write and list consistency, trustworthy store persistence, aligned clocks within the lease margin, properly restricted deployment writes, and a supervisor for production node fencing.</p></Card><Card title="Not supplied by this protocol" icon="alert"><p>Exactly-once external effects, cross-actor atomic commit, arbitrary-delay proof of read linearizability, durable guest memory, a globally atomic code rollout, built-in workload schedulers, an audit-log retention guarantee, or unlimited availability during partitions.</p></Card></div>
      <p>The diagrams explain the implementation and its intended contract. They do not certify a distributed-systems proof or production readiness. In particular, no-segment calls skip post-upload fencing checks, renewal/fence notification is asynchronous, and the retry window is not an absolute deadline.</p>
    </Section>
